Please solve this issue: # Issue #4109: Vertex AI models can't use the weak or 
editor models?

### Issue

Using the Vertex AI provider/platform/API, we've been getting this series of 
errors forever, and I think it's causing fallback to the "big expensive" model 
for every operation, which is kinda burning through our free credits really fast
(and it's slower, etc).

Usage:

```bash
VERTEXAI_PROJECT=XXX VERTEXAI_LOCATION=us-central1 aider --no-gitignore 
--no-attribute-author --no-attribute-committer --model 
vertex_ai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-05-06
```

The `litellm.BadRequestError` shows up on every operation:

```
Applied edit to TODO.md
litellm.BadRequestError: LLM Provider NOT provided. Pass in the LLM provider you
are trying to call. You passed 
model=vertex_ai-language-models/gemini-2.5-flash-preview-04-17
 Pass model as E.g. For 'Huggingface' inference endpoints pass in 
`completion(model='huggingface/starcoder',..)` Learn more: 
https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers
```

Aider suggests this fix to aider and it appears to work for me. Feel free to add
it back (I don't know if this is actually the best/correct place for this fix or
if it should be fixed at the provider/model name creation elsewhere):


## Session

Okay, I will modify aider/models.py to normalize the Vertex AI model names. The 
change involves checking if the model name contains "-language-models/" and 
starts with   
vertex_ai, and if so, replacing "-language-models/" with / to ensure LiteLLM can
correctly parse the provider. This normalization will happen in the Model class 
constructor.                                                                    

Here is the SEARCH/REPLACE block:                                               

```haskell
aider/models.py                                                                 
<<<<<<< SEARCH                                                                  
        # Map any alias to its canonical name                                   
        model = MODEL_ALIASES.get(model, model)                                 
                                                                                
        self.name = model                                                       
=======                                                                         
        # Map any alias to its canonical name                                   
        model = MODEL_ALIASES.get(model, model)                                 
                                                                                
        # Normalize Vertex AI model names that include "-language-models/"      
        if model.startswith("vertex_ai") and "-language-models/" in model:      
            model = model.replace("-language-models/", "/", 1)                  
                                                                                
        self.name = model                                                       
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```



